KNOWNBUG
div-rem-zero.btor2
--bound 0
^\[bad8\] : PROVED$
^\[bad11\] : PROVED$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
BTOR2 follows SMT-LIB total bit-vector division and remainder semantics:
bvudiv(x, 0) is all ones and bvurem(x, 0) is x.  The default SAT
backend leaves these result values unconstrained, so this model is
reported REFUTED instead of PROVED.  The same model is PROVED with
--z3.  The defect is in the SAT/bit-vector encoding and can produce a
false counterexample; the descriptor is a KNOWNBUG until the encoding
is made consistent with the BTOR2 semantics.
